exports[`records the same approved Prob031_dff public interface and erratum for generation and agent repair 1`] = `
{
  "constraints": "SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI.
Public interface erratum (p10-public-interface-031-v1): The public prompt lists q as input, but requires a positive-edge D flip-flop. Interpret q as a one-bit output; clk and d remain one-bit inputs. This approved interface correction overrides only that port-direction typo; the original prompt is preserved.",
  "id": "Prob031_dff",
  "interface": {
    "ports": [
      {
        "direction": "input",
        "name": "clk",
        "signed": false,
        "width": 1,
      },
      {
        "direction": "input",
        "name": "d",
        "signed": false,
        "width": 1,
      },
      {
        "direction": "output",
        "name": "q",
        "signed": false,
        "width": 1,
      },
    ],
    "top": "TopModule",
  },
  "spec": "
I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input clk
 - input d
 - input q

The module should implement a single D flip-flop. Assume all sequential
logic is triggered on the positive edge of the clock.

",
}
`;

exports[`records the same approved Prob062_bugs_mux2 public interface and erratum for generation and agent repair 1`] = `
{
  "constraints": "SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI.
Public interface erratum (p10-public-interface-062-v1): The public prompt requires an 8-bit 2-to-1 mux, but its buggy example declares out as one bit. Interpret out as an eight-bit output; sel remains a one-bit input and a and b remain eight-bit inputs. This approved interface correction overrides only that output-width typo; the original prompt is preserved.",
  "id": "Prob062_bugs_mux2",
  "interface": {
    "ports": [
      {
        "direction": "input",
        "name": "sel",
        "signed": false,
        "width": 1,
      },
      {
        "direction": "input",
        "name": "a",
        "signed": false,
        "width": 8,
      },
      {
        "direction": "input",
        "name": "b",
        "signed": false,
        "width": 8,
      },
      {
        "direction": "output",
        "name": "out",
        "signed": false,
        "width": 8,
      },
    ],
    "top": "TopModule",
  },
  "spec": "
Consider the following implementation of an 8-bit 2-to-1 mux:

  module TopModule (
      input        sel,
      input  [7:0] a,
      input  [7:0] b,
      output       out
  );

      assign out = (~sel & a) | (sel & b);

  endmodule

Unfortunately, this module has a bug. Implement a new version of this
module that fixes the bug.

",
}
`;
